PARITY: 1:1 port of web/src/features/driving/components/drive-detail/MoreDetailsPanel.tsx.
  - Data: useTranslation -> P1/S10 i18n catalog (13 driveDetail.* keys); useUnits + global fmtNumber
    precision/locale -> P1/S8 SettingsStore via UnitPreferences.fromSettings (distance/speed/temperature units +
    precision + locale). No HTTP in the view; the host threads a UiState<MoreDetailsSnapshot>.
  - Shared components: @/components/ui GlassPanel + @/components/motion FadeIn mapped to the native GlassPanel +
    FadeIn; PanelTitle/Icon/Caption-equivalent + feedback EmptyState/ErrorDisplay/Skeleton + DataFreshness.
  - SI-canonical: odometer/range/distance (m), min speed (m/s) and temperatures (degC) carried as SI and
    converted at the Compose boundary via convert{Distance,Speed,Temp}FromSI; energy (Wh/kWh threshold), power
    (kW), elevation (m) and the battery delta (%) carried in the web stats display unit. Consumption derives
    energyWh/(distanceM/1000) and applies the web toEfficiencyDisplay (* 1.609344 for miles).
  - States: every state renders - loading skeleton grids, hard error + retry (QueryError equivalent), friendly
    empty state, content, and stale/offline cached "last known" with a freshness chip + auto-refresh. @Preview
    entry points exercise Content / Offline / Loading / Empty / Error.
  - i18n: all 13 driveDetail.* labels + common.noData resolve through stringResource; no English literal in code.
  - a11y: each cell is one TalkBack node ("label, value"); elevation announces directional arrows; reduce-motion
    honored via the shared FadeIn; font-scale-safe Material 3 typography roles.
  - Tests: adapter (settings -> prefs), SI->display projection incl. imperial/fahrenheit/precision boundaries,
    conditional temperature cells, '-'/'?' guards, kWh-vs-Wh threshold, per-state classifier (loading/content/
    empty/offline), label + announcement (a11y-key) coverage, and the PII-safe view.opened diagnostic.

CAPABILITY: Jetpack Compose + Material 3 + Kotlin toolchain present and exercised (assembleRelease produced the
